  "title": "Election Commission of India Faces Controversy Over SIR Revisions and Protests",
  "summary": "The Election Commission (EC) of India faced criticism over its handling of Special Intensive Revision (SIR) orders following allegations of procedural issues. Congress demanded immediate action to address concerns, including the suspension of a controversial SIR exercise, while the Commission defended its processes and claimed the changes to electoral rolls were upheld by legal standards.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Election Commission of India faced criticism over its handling of Special Intensive Revision (SIR) orders following allegations of procedural issues.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The EC extended the objections period for SIR decisions and introduced a new format for declarations with Form 6, while noting that only specific cases require personal hearings.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The EC suspended a controversial SIR exercise, with Congress demanding immediate action to address concerns.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
